<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.2: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01277</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2baa0c2d-83d4-4cbc-8e4d-64d4af74f059</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Olivia has two different job offers for babysitting next Saturday.</para>
<list>
  <item>Job 1: She will receive $5 for accepting the job, then $10 for every hour she works.</item>
  <item>Job 2: She will receive $1.50 for accepting the job, $3 after the first hour, $6 after the second hour, and for each additional hour her pay per hour will double.</item>
</list>
<para>Olivia can only work 3 hours. How much would she make at each job?</para></section>
</content>
</document>
